{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794539572780,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc256ffeoTwd6NrNr3Yljs","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2e4cc38001EPvFhJyfbPtn0S","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc256ffeoTwd6NrNr3Yljs","messageID":"msg_1d2e4a2cf001PHqBXoWnKGcnWe","type":"tool","id":"call_3f34c971775f4d709e512687","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli/deep-research-strategy.md, lines 1-233\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Research Strategy - cross-cli command surfacing\n3: description: Cross-CLI usefulness angle for command surfacing after planned phases 005-008.\n4: ---\n5: \n6: # Deep Research Strategy - cross-cli\n7: \n8: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n9: \n10: ### Purpose\n11: \n12: Establish, per runtime (claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh), whether a model starts an advisor-offered command, what stops it, and which post-005-008 change raises the start rate for the least work.\n13: \n14: ### Usage\n15: \n16: - Reads evidence from the parent packet (`008-command-surfacing-build`) and the pre-arm behaviour log.\n17: - Writes only inside the lineage directory.\n18: - Reducer owns Sections 3, 6, 7-11A.\n19: \n20: ### Question Injection Surface\n21: \n22: `inbox.jsonl` in this lineage directory if an external question appears.\n23: \n24: ---\n25: \n26: ## 2. TOPIC\n27: Cross-CLI command surfacing after planned phases 005-008: per-runtime evidence of whether a model starts an offered advisor command, what stops it, and which fix raises start rate.\n28: \n29: ---\n30: \n31: <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n32: ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n33: - [x] Which hook or pointer surface must each of the six runtimes have before an advisor recommendation is even offered, and which runtimes are unwired in the pre-arm log?\n34: - [x] Why does the model start so few offered commands on each runtime (claude 3/12, codex 0/12, pi 0/12, devin 2/11, opencode 3/7, dsh 2/7), and what does the missing COMMAND line prove about the brief?\n35: - [x] Which change to the brief contract or hook wiring raises start rate per runtime, and how does it extend rather than duplicate planned phases 005-008?\n36: - [x] How must command files be laid out and installed so a fresh external repository exposes every command on every runtime, given the g5 skill.md folder-shadowing result?\n37: - [x] What is the cheapest reliable way to measure start rate across six runtimes without running pi, ollama, or the full test suite?\n38: \n39: <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n40: \n41: ---\n42: \n43: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n44: \n45: - Re-recommending what phases 005-008 already plan.\n46: - Implementing any fix (research only).\n47: - The UX and performance angles owned by sibling lineages, except where they change per-runtime start behaviour.\n48: - Re-running pi, starting or stopping ollama, or running the full vitest suite.\n49: - Reading or printing holdout-split rows from command-prompts.jsonl.\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n54: \n55: - Max 5 iterations, convergence threshold 0.05 after the 3-iteration floor.\n56: - Stop early only at legal convergence; record the reason in research.md.\n57: - No writes outside this lineage directory; spec.md writeback and continuity save are deferred and recorded as scope decisions.\n58: \n59: ---\n60: \n61: <!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n62: ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n63: - Which hook or pointer surface must each of the six runtimes have before an advisor recommendation is even offered, and which runtimes are unwired in the pre-arm log?\n64: - Why does the model start so few offered commands on each runtime (claude 3/12, codex 0/12, pi 0/12, devin 2/11, opencode 3/7, dsh 2/7), and what does the missing COMMAND line prove about the brief?\n65: - Which change to the brief contract or hook wiring raises start rate per runtime, and how does it extend rather than duplicate planned phases 005-008?\n66: - How must command files be laid out and installed so a fresh external repository exposes every command on every runtime, given the g5 skill.md folder-shadowing result?\n67: - What is the cheapest reliable way to measure start rate across six runtimes without running pi, ollama, or the full test suite?\n68: \n69: <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n70: \n71: ---\n72: \n73: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n74: <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n75: ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n76: - scoring the log before reading plans exposed that the baseline measures the wrong thing; the plan's own ADR-002 confirms it. Reading each runtime's shim rather than assuming \"not wired\" avoided a wrong root cause. (iteration 1)\n77: - checking the raw transcript against the normalized one exposed a blind spot the scorer design hides; reading the runner's argv exposed the Codex trust gap that a rate alone would have blamed on the model. (iteration 2)\n78: - reading the install guide as a user would exposed two production blockers (Codex approval, DSH absence) that a repo-internal view hides; the renderer's existing `runtime` option made the head change cheap enough to rank. (iteration 3)\n79: \n80: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n81: \n82: ---\n83: \n84: <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n85: ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n86: - no exported per-run score prevented an exact uncapped rate; the bound is the honest substitute. (iteration 1)\n87: - the G5 artifact could not be tied to the real mirror path; the verification is named instead of assumed. (iteration 2)\n88: - no artifact exists for failed host-command invocations, so that path stays a gap. (iteration 3)\n89: \n90: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n91: \n92: ---\n93: \n94: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n95: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n96: ### **\"A `COMMAND:` line proves the model saw an offer.\"** DSH emitted two `COMMAND:` tokens in six sampled sessions with no advisor row enabled, so the token can appear without a brief. [SOURCE: .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs:53] -- BLOCKED (iteration 2, 1 attempts)\n97: - What was tried: **\"A `COMMAND:` line proves the model saw an offer.\"** DSH emitted two `COMMAND:` tokens in six sampled sessions with no advisor row enabled, so the token can appear without a brief. [SOURCE: .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs:53]\n98: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n99: - Do NOT retry: **\"A `COMMAND:` line proves the model saw an offer.\"** DSH emitted two `COMMAND:` tokens in six sampled sessions with no advisor row enabled, so the token can appear without a brief. [SOURCE: .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs:53]\n100: \n101: ### **\"Add the document path to every runtime's brief.\"** Unnecessary token cost on Claude and OpenCode, which can resolve the command through their own surfaces; the change is worth it only on hosts with no registry. -- BLOCKED (iteration 3, 1 attempts)\n102: - What was tried: **\"Add the document path to every runtime's brief.\"** Unnecessary token cost on Claude and OpenCode, which can resolve the command through their own surfaces; the change is worth it only on hosts with no registry.\n103: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n104: - Do NOT retry: **\"Add the document path to every runtime's brief.\"** Unnecessary token cost on Claude and OpenCode, which can resolve the command through their own surfaces; the change is worth it only on hosts with no registry.\n105: \n106: ### **\"Codex declined the command.\"** It never received a brief in the arena: hooks are unapproved there and no `Advisor:` line exists in any sampled Codex transcript. [SOURCE: .codex/README.md:54] -- BLOCKED (iteration 2, 1 attempts)\n107: - What was tried: **\"Codex declined the command.\"** It never received a brief in the arena: hooks are unapproved there and no `Advisor:` line exists in any sampled Codex transcript. [SOURCE: .codex/README.md:54]\n108: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n109: - Do NOT retry: **\"Codex declined the command.\"** It never received a brief in the arena: hooks are unapproved there and no `Advisor:` line exists in any sampled Codex transcript. [SOURCE: .codex/README.md:54]\n110: \n111: ### **\"Ship 005 and 006 and the start rate rises.\"** That is the planned path and cannot be recommended; it is also unverifiable until the two measurement facts exist. The recommendations above are what remains after those phases. -- BLOCKED (iteration 3, 1 attempts)\n112: - What was tried: **\"Ship 005 and 006 and the start rate rises.\"** That is the planned path and cannot be recommended; it is also unverifiable until the two measurement facts exist. The recommendations above are what remains after those phases.\n113: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n114: - Do NOT retry: **\"Ship 005 and 006 and the start rate rises.\"** That is the planned path and cannot be recommended; it is also unverifiable until the two measurement facts exist. The recommendations above are what remains after those phases.\n115: \n116: ### **\"The hook is not wired on most runtimes.\"** False: five of six have a live delivery path in the repo, and Codex/Devin proxy the same adapter as Claude. Wiring alone does not explain the rates. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.ts:22] -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n117: - What was tried: **\"The hook is not wired on most runtimes.\"** False: five of six have a live delivery path in the repo, and Codex/Devin proxy the same adapter as Claude. Wiring alone does not explain the rates. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.ts:22]\n118: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n119: - Do NOT retry: **\"The hook is not wired on most runtimes.\"** False: five of six have a live delivery path in the repo, and Codex/Devin proxy the same adapter as Claude. Wiring alone does not explain the rates. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.ts:22]\n120: \n121: ### **\"The hook is too slow, so the brief is dropped.\"** Not supported by the measured data: median hook latency is about 200 ms against a 2,500 ms budget, and a warm embed is 6.57 ms median. Cold-start cost is real but unmeasured; it is not the observed cause. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt:40] [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt:12] -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n122: - What was tried: **\"The hook is too slow, so the brief is dropped.\"** Not supported by the measured data: median hook latency is about 200 ms against a 2,500 ms budget, and a warm embed is 6.57 ms median. Cold-start cost is real but unmeasured; it is not the observed cause. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt:40] [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt:12]\n123: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n124: - Do NOT retry: **\"The hook is too slow, so the brief is dropped.\"** Not supported by the measured data: median hook latency is about 200 ms against a 2,500 ms budget, and a warm embed is 6.57 ms median. Cold-start cost is real but unmeasured; it is not the observed cause. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt:40] [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt:12]\n125: \n126: ### A G5 fix cannot be verified from the existing artifacts; the definitive listing needs a throwaway repo and a temporary `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`. Recording it as the verification step is more honest than treating the stand-in folder as the real path. -- BLOCKED (iteration 2, 1 attempts)\n127: - What was tried: A G5 fix cannot be verified from the existing artifacts; the definitive listing needs a throwaway repo and a temporary `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`. Recording it as the verification step is more honest than treating the stand-in folder as the real path.\n128: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n129: - Do NOT retry: A G5 fix cannot be verified from the existing artifacts; the definitive listing needs a throwaway repo and a temporary `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`. Recording it as the verification step is more honest than treating the stand-in folder as the real path.\n130: \n131: ### Cursor is out of scope: its reader is gated, so it is reported as not measured by design. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/plan.md:81] -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n132: - What was tried: Cursor is out of scope: its reader is gated, so it is reported as not measured by design. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/plan.md:81]\n133: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n134: - Do NOT retry: Cursor is out of scope: its reader is gated, so it is reported as not measured by design. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/plan.md:81]\n135: \n136: ### No existing artifact measures a failed host-command invocation (for example a Codex `/create:readme` typed into an exec turn). The scorer sees tool calls and text, not a rejected slash token, so this gap is recorded rather than guessed. -- BLOCKED (iteration 3, 1 attempts)\n137: - What was tried: No existing artifact measures a failed host-command invocation (for example a Codex `/create:readme` typed into an exec turn). The scorer sees tool calls and text, not a rejected slash token, so this gap is recorded rather than guessed.\n138: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n139: - Do NOT retry: No existing artifact measures a failed host-command invocation (for example a Codex `/create:readme` typed into an exec turn). The scorer sees tool calls and text, not a rejected slash token, so this gap is recorded rather than guessed.\n140: \n141: ### Recounting starts from run-log rows alone cannot separate capped from started per row, because the scorer's per-run result is not exported. The honest output is the bound in Finding 3, not an exact uncapped rate. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n142: - What was tried: Recounting starts from run-log rows alone cannot separate capped from started per row, because the scorer's per-run result is not exported. The honest output is the bound in Finding 3, not an exact uncapped rate.\n143: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n144: - Do NOT retry: Recounting starts from run-log rows alone cannot separate capped from started per row, because the scorer's per-run result is not exported. The honest output is the bound in Finding 3, not an exact uncapped rate.\n145: \n146: ### The scorer's `normalize` discards hook context for Claude, so post-processing transcripts cannot recover \"was it offered\" without either reading raw prompt records (runtime-specific) or recording the brief at hook time. -- BLOCKED (iteration 2, 1 attempts)\n147: - What was tried: The scorer's `normalize` discards hook context for Claude, so post-processing transcripts cannot recover \"was it offered\" without either reading raw prompt records (runtime-specific) or recording the brief at hook time.\n148: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n149: - Do NOT retry: The scorer's `normalize` discards hook context for Claude, so post-processing transcripts cannot recover \"was it offered\" without either reading raw prompt records (runtime-specific) or recording the brief at hook time.\n150: \n151: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n152: \n153: ---\n154: \n155: <!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n156: ## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n157: - **\"The hook is not wired on most runtimes.\"** False: five of six have a live delivery path in the repo, and Codex/Devin proxy the same adapter as Claude. Wiring alone does not explain the rates. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/codex/user-prompt-submit.ts:22] (iteration 1)\n158: - **\"The hook is too slow, so the brief is dropped.\"** Not supported by the measured data: median hook latency is about 200 ms against a 2,500 ms budget, and a warm embed is 6.57 ms median. Cold-start cost is real but unmeasured; it is not the observed cause. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt:40] [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt:12] (iteration 1)\n159: - Cursor is out of scope: its reader is gated, so it is reported as not measured by design. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/plan.md:81] (iteration 1)\n160: - Recounting starts from run-log rows alone cannot separate capped from started per row, because the scorer's per-run result is not exported. The honest output is the bound in Finding 3, not an exact uncapped rate. (iteration 1)\n161: - **\"A `COMMAND:` line proves the model saw an offer.\"** DSH emitted two `COMMAND:` tokens in six sampled sessions with no advisor row enabled, so the token can appear without a brief. [SOURCE: .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/index.mjs:53] (iteration 2)\n162: - **\"Codex declined the command.\"** It never received a brief in the arena: hooks are unapproved there and no `Advisor:` line exists in any sampled Codex transcript. [SOURCE: .codex/README.md:54] (iteration 2)\n163: - A G5 fix cannot be verified from the existing artifacts; the definitive listing needs a throwaway repo and a temporary `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`. Recording it as the verification step is more honest than treating the stand-in folder as the real path. (iteration 2)\n164: - The scorer's `normalize` discards hook context for Claude, so post-processing transcripts cannot recover \"was it offered\" without either reading raw prompt records (runtime-specific) or recording the brief at hook time. (iteration 2)\n165: - **\"Add the document path to every runtime's brief.\"** Unnecessary token cost on Claude and OpenCode, which can resolve the command through their own surfaces; the change is worth it only on hosts with no registry. (iteration 3)\n166: - **\"Ship 005 and 006 and the start rate rises.\"** That is the planned path and cannot be recommended; it is also unverifiable until the two measurement facts exist. The recommendations above are what remains after those phases. (iteration 3)\n167: - No existing artifact measures a failed host-command invocation (for example a Codex `/create:readme` typed into an exec turn). The scorer sees tool calls and text, not a rejected slash token, so this gap is recorded rather than guessed. (iteration 3)\n168: \n169: <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n170: \n171: ---\n172: \n173: <!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n174: ## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n175: - Completed pivots: 0\n176: - Failed pivots: 0\n177: - Audited overrides: 0\n178: - Saturated: none yet\n179: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n180: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n181: \n182: <!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n183: \n184: ---\n185: \n186: <!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n187: ## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n188: [None yet]\n189: \n190: <!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n191: \n192: ---\n193: \n194: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n195: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n196: [All tracked questions are resolved]\n197: \n198: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n199: \n200: ---\n201: \n202: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n203: ## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n204: \n205: Evidence pointers (read-only):\n206: \n207: - `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md`, `decision-record.md`, `goal.md`.\n208: - Child plans/tasks: `005-recommendation-contract-and-brief`, `006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers`, `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof`, `008-embedder-setup-and-cost`.\n209: - `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl` scored with `score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary` (baseline: claude 3/12, codex 0/12, pi 0/12, devin 2/11, opencode 3/7, dsh 2/7; COMMAND line 0 everywhere).\n210: - `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/g5/result.txt` (skill.md shadows sibling commands as one Skill entry on Claude Code).\n211: - `008-embedder-setup-and-cost/scratch/measured-2026-11-12.txt` and `measure-embedder-cost.mjs`.\n212: - Runtime hook/pointer surfaces under `.claude/`, `.codex/`, `.opencode/`, `.pi/`, `.devin/`, `.dsh/`, and the advisor runtime `runtime/` tree.\n213: \n214: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n215: \n216: - Source pointers: advisor hook, brief renderer, gate-2 binding, runtime pointer installers.\n217: - Reuse candidates: existing scorer `score-command-transcripts.mjs`, existing hooks.\n218: - Integration points: hook brief text, command file layout, per-runtime config.\n219: - Constraints: planned-not-built phases, read-only git, no pi/ollama.\n220: \n221: ---\n222: \n223: ## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n224: - Max iterations: 5\n225: - Convergence threshold: 0.05\n226: - Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n227: - Progressive synthesis: true\n228: - research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n229: - Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred)\n230: - Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\n231: - Canonical pause sentinel: `.deep-research-pause`\n232: - Current generation: 1\n233: - Started: 2026-11-12T22:50:26.300Z","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli/deep-research-strategy.md, lines 1-233\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Research Strategy - cross-cli command surfacing\n3: description: Cross-CLI usefulness angle for command surfacing after planned phases 005-008.\n4: ---\n5: \n6: # Deep Research Strategy - cross-cli\n7: \n8: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n9: \n10: ### Purpose\n11: \n12: Establish, per runtime (claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh), whether a model starts an advisor-offered command, what stops it, and which post-005-008 change raises the start rate for the least work.\n13: \n14: ### Usage\n15: \n16: - Reads evidence from the parent packet (`008-command-surfacing-build`) and the pre-arm behaviour log.\n17: - Writes only inside the lineage directory.\n18: - Reducer owns Sections 3, 6, 7-11A.\n19: \n20: ### Question Injection Surface\n21: \n22: `inbox.jsonl` in this lineage directory if an external question appears.\n23: \n24: ---\n25: \n26: ## 2. TOPIC\n27: Cross-CLI command surfacing after planned phases 005-008: per-runtime evidence of whether a model starts an offered advisor command, what stops it, and which fix raises start rate.\n28: \n29: ---\n30: \n31: <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n32: ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n33: - [x] Which hook or pointer surface must each of the six runtimes have before an advisor recommendation is even offered, and which runtimes are unwired in the pre-arm log?\n34: - [x] Why does the model start so few offered commands on each runtime (claude 3/12, codex 0/12, pi 0/12, devin 2/11, opencode 3/7, dsh 2/7), and what does the missing COMMAND line prove about the brief?\n35: - [x] Which change to the brief contract or hook wiring raises start rate per runtime, and how does it extend rather than duplicate planned phases 005-008?\n36: - [x] How must command files be laid out and installed so a fresh external repository exposes every command on every runtime, given the g5 skill.md folder-shadowing result?\n37: - [x] What is the cheapest reliable way to measure start rate across six runtimes without running pi, ollama, or the full test suite?\n38: \n39: <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n40: \n41: ---\n42: \n43: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n44: \n45: - Re-recommending what phases 005-008 already plan.\n46: - Implementing any fix (research only).\n47: - The UX and performance angles owned by sibling lineages, except where they change per-runtime start behaviour.\n48: - Re-running pi, starting or stopping ollama, or running the full vitest suite.\n49: - Reading or printing holdout-split rows from command-prompts.jsonl.\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n54: \n55: - Max 5 iterations, convergence threshold 0.05 after the 3-iteration floor.\n56: - Stop early only at legal convergence; record the reason in research.md.\n57: - No writes outside this lineage directory; spec.md writeback and continuity save are deferred and recorded as scope decisions.\n58: \n59: ---\n60: \n61: <!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n62: ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n63: - Which hook or pointer surface must each of the six runtimes have before an advisor recommendation is even offered, and which runtimes are unwired in the pre-arm log?\n64: - Why does the model start so few offered commands on each runtime (claude 3/12, codex 0/12, pi 0/12, devin 2/11, opencode 3/7, dsh 2/7), and what does the missing COMMAND line prove about the brief?\n65: - Which change to the brief contract or hook wiring raises start rate per runtime, and how does it extend rather than duplicate planned phases 005-008?\n66: - How must command files be laid out and installed so a fresh external repository exposes every command on every runtime, given the g5 skill.md folder-shadowing result?\n67: - What is the cheapest reliable way to measure start rate across six runtimes without running pi, ollama, or the full test suite?\n68: \n69: <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n70: \n71: ---\n72: \n73: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n74: <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n75: ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n76: - scoring the log before reading plans exposed that the baseline measures the wrong thing; the plan's own ADR-002 confirms it. Reading each runtime's shim rather than assuming \"not wired\" avoided a wrong root cause. (iteration 1)\n77: - checking the raw transcript against the normalized one exposed a blind spot the scorer design hides; reading the runner's argv exposed the Codex trust gap that a rate alone would have blamed on the model. (iteration 2)\n78: - reading the install guide as a user would exposed two production blockers (Codex approval, DSH absence) that a repo-internal view hides; the renderer's existing `runtime` option made the head change cheap enough to rank. (iteration 3)\n79: \n80: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n81: \n82: ---\n83: \n84: <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n85: ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n86: - no exported per-run score prevented an exact uncapped rate; the bound is the honest substitute. (iteration 1)\n87: - the G5 artifact could not be tied to the real mirror path; the verification is named instead of assumed. (iteration 2)\n88: - no artifact exists for failed host-command invocations, so that path stays a gap. (iteration 3)\n89: \n90: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n91: \n92: ---\n93: \n94: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n95: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n96: