{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794539730641,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc256ffeoTwd6NrNr3Yljs","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2e72ff1002Kb0zmDfmFRwnKe","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc256ffeoTwd6NrNr3Yljs","messageID":"msg_1d2e71db1001qibjVPzTV10Ymc","type":"tool","id":"call_00_eNZwShuHGF6VPK4EwDN10182","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && node -e '\nconst fs=require(\"fs\");\nconst base=\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/\";\nconst a=fs.readFileSync(base+\"runs-post-final.jsonl\",\"utf8\").trim().split(\"\\n\").map(JSON.parse).filter(r=>r.runtime===\"claude\");\nconst b=fs.readFileSync(base+\"runs-post-claude-bullet.jsonl\",\"utf8\").trim().split(\"\\n\").map(JSON.parse).filter(r=>r.runtime===\"claude\");\nconst key=r=>r.rowId; const bm=new Map(b.map(r=>[key(r),r]));\nlet diff=0;\nfor(const r of a){const o=bm.get(key(r)); if(!o){console.log(\"missing\",key(r));continue;} if(JSON.stringify([r.exit,r.offeredCommand,r.offeredPolicy,r.briefDelivered])!==JSON.stringify([o.exit,o.offeredCommand,o.offeredPolicy,o.briefDelivered])){diff++;console.log(key(r),\"final\",r.exit,r.offeredCommand,r.offeredPolicy,r.briefDelivered,\"| bullet\",o.exit,o.offeredCommand,o.offeredPolicy,o.briefDelivered);}}\nconsole.log(\"claude rows\",a.length,b.length,\"diffs\",diff);\nconsole.log(\"bullet file locators sample:\",JSON.stringify(b[0]?.locator?.projectDir));\nconsole.log(\"final file locators sample:\",JSON.stringify(a[0]?.locator?.projectDir));\n'"},"output":"claude rows 24 24 diffs 0\nbullet file locators sample: \"/private/var/folders/3c/zfqcqsts0kn19cgblj82gqhm0000gn/T/skilled-behaviour-arenas/post-claude\"\nfinal file locators sample: \"/private/var/folders/3c/zfqcqsts0kn19cgblj82gqhm0000gn/T/skilled-behaviour-arenas/post-claude\"\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"claude rows 24 24 diffs 0\nbullet file locators sample: \"/private/var/folders/3c/zfqcqsts0kn19cgblj82gqhm0000gn/T/skilled-behaviour-arenas/post-claude\"\nfinal file locators sample: \"/private/var/folders/3c/zfqcqsts0kn19cgblj82gqhm0000gn/T/skilled-behaviour-arenas/post-claude\"\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && node -e '\\nconst fs=require(\\\"fs\\\");\\nconst base=\\\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/\\\";\\nconst a=fs.readFileSync(base+\\\"runs-post-final.jsonl\\\",\\\"utf8\\\").trim().split(\\\"\\\\n\\\").map(JSON.parse).filter(r=>r.runtime===\\\"claude\\\");\\nconst b=fs.readFileSync(base+\\\"runs-post-claude-bullet.jsonl\\\",\\\"utf8\\\").trim().split(\\\"\\\\n\\\").map(JSON.parse).filter(r=>r.runtime===\\\"claude\\\");\\nconst key=r=>r.rowId; const bm=new Map(b.map(r=>[key(r),r]));\\nlet diff=0;\\nfor(const r of a){const o=bm.get(key(r)); if(!o){console.log(\\\"missing\\\",key(r));continue;} if(JSON.stringify([r.exit,r.offeredCommand,r.offeredPolicy,r.briefDelivered])!==JSON.stringify([o.exit,o.offeredCommand,o.offeredPolicy,o.briefDelivered])){diff++;console.log(key(r),\\\"final\\\",r.exit,r.offeredCommand,r.offeredPolicy,r.briefDelivered,\\\"| bullet\\\",o.exit,o.offeredCommand,o.offeredPolicy,o.briefDelivered);}}\\nconsole.log(\\\"claude rows\\\",a.length,b.length,\\\"diffs\\\",diff);\\nconsole.log(\\\"bullet file locators sample:\\\",JSON.stringify(b[0]?.locator?.projectDir));\\nconsole.log(\\\"final file locators sample:\\\",JSON.stringify(a[0]?.locator?.projectDir));\\n'\"}"},"time":{"start":1794539728881,"end":1794539730641}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794539732331,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc256ffeoTwd6NrNr3Yljs","part":{"id":"prt_1d2e73d6b001s9hqs1bOQP3irA","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc256ffeoTwd6NrNr3Yljs","messageID":"msg_1d2e71db1001qibjVPzTV10Ymc","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"9c4b03388cb1333e39865d7f555fe1b09d6da2c1","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":986,"output":541,"reasoning":615,"cache":{"read":112256,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794539735042,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc256ffeoTwd6NrNr3Yljs","part":{"id":"prt_1d2e74802001iAug3k18XC1Sp9","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc256ffeoTwd6NrNr3Yljs","messageID":"msg_1d2e73d6f001u6TLbvEhOaM320","type":"step-start","snapshot":"9c4b03388cb1333e39865d7f555fe1b09d6da2c1"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794539736593,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc256ffeoTwd6NrNr3Yljs","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2e74c06001KEbkisv8weIx7X","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc256ffeoTwd6NrNr3Yljs","messageID":"msg_1d2e73d6f001u6TLbvEhOaM320","type":"tool","id":"call_01_2wOISEk7eIdjRTX8iY4X5536","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '30,80p' .codex/README.md; echo \"=== hooks.json ===\"; cat .codex/hooks.json 2>/dev/null | head -40"},"output":"\nEach generator deletes any output it no longer expects, so a removed command or agent leaves no stale copy behind. The `config.toml` file is the one file here that no generator writes. It turns hooks on and sets up the Code Mode server.\n\n---\n\n## 2. HOW IT CONNECTS TO SKILLED\n\n| Piece | How Codex gets it |\n|---|---|\n| Instructions | The root [`AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md), the shared instruction file for every runtime |\n| Skills | No skills folder here. The advisor brief on each prompt names the skill to load, and the skill files load from `.skilled/skills/` |\n| Agents | Each shared agent as a TOML file in `agents/`, written by `sync-agents.cjs`. Each file carries the full agent text |\n| Commands | One prompt stub per command in `prompts/`, written by `sync-prompts.cjs`. A command such as `create/agent` becomes `create-agent`, and the stub tells Codex to read the canonical file in full |\n| Hooks and guards | `hooks.json`, rendered from the shared hook registry. The hooks cover the advisor, the spec-folder gate, the dispatch and MCP route guards, the post-edit checks and the session context. Each command falls back to a message when its adapter is missing |\n| Advisor | The advisor runs on the prompt hook and names the skill for each request |\n| MCP | The Code Mode server is written inline in `config.toml` |\n| Goals | No goal hook in the registry. The `create-goal` prompt authors a packet's `goal.md`, but Codex gets no session goal command here |\n| Dispatch | [`cli-codex`](../.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/README.md) hands work to Codex from another runtime. Its [hook contract](../.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/references/hook-contract.md) lists every hook a dispatched session runs |\n\n---\n\n## 3. GETTING STARTED\n\n1. Open the repository in Codex from its root. Codex reads `hooks.json` from this checkout once the checkout is trusted.\n2. Approve the hooks. Codex runs a project hook only after you approve that exact entry. Open `/hooks` in an interactive session and approve each entry it lists for review. The approval is stored as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again.\n3. Check the global file. `~/.codex/hooks.json` must hold no copy of these entries, or each hook runs twice. Run `install-codex-hooks.mjs --check` to confirm that it holds no stale copy.\n\n---\n\n## 4. WHAT IS GENERATED AND WHAT IS AUTHORED\n\n| Path | Kind | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `agents/*.toml` | Generated | Written by `sync-agents.cjs`. The sandbox mode and model settings are set here and cannot be read back into `.skilled/` |\n| `prompts/*.md` | Generated | Written by `sync-prompts.cjs`. Each stub points at its canonical command file |\n| `hooks.json` | Generated | Rendered from `hook-registry.json` by `sync-hook-registrations.cjs` |\n| `hooks/` | Links | A discovery mirror of the scripts that `hooks.json` runs |\n| `config.toml` | Authored | Turns hooks on and writes the Code Mode server inline. No generator writes it |\n| `repo-rules`, `manual-testing-playbook` | Links | The rule files and the `cli-codex` playbook |\n| `README.md`, `SYNC.md` | Authored | The documentation |\n\n**The one rule:** never edit a generated file here. Change the source in `.skilled/`, or change `hook-registry.json` for hooks, then rerun the matching generator. A hand edit to `hooks.json` is overwritten by the next sync.\n\n---\n\n## 5. CHECKING IT IS HEALTHY\n\n```bash\nnode .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-agents.cjs --check\nnode .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-prompts.cjs --check\nnode .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-hook-registrations.cjs --check\n=== hooks.json ===\n{\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"SessionStart\": [\n      {\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"bash -c 'cd \\\"${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\\\" && node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/codex/session-start.js || { printf \\\"%s\\\\n\\\" \\\"mk-hook-drift host=codex event=SessionStart adapter=session-start.js\\\" >&2; printf %s \\\"{\\\\\\\"hookSpecificOutput\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"hookEventName\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"SessionStart\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"additionalContext\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"mk codex hook could not resolve; build the spec-kit runtime (npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit run build) or restore the missing adapter\\\\\\\"}}\\\"; }'\",\n            \"timeout\": 3\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"bash -c 'cd \\\"${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\\\" && bash .skilled/bin/worktree-guard.sh || { printf \\\"%s\\\\n\\\" \\\"mk-hook-drift host=codex event=SessionStart adapter=worktree-guard.sh\\\" >&2; printf %s \\\"{\\\\\\\"hookSpecificOutput\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"hookEventName\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"SessionStart\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"additionalContext\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"mk codex hook could not resolve; build the spec-kit runtime (npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit run build) or restore the missing adapter\\\\\\\"}}\\\"; }'\",\n            \"timeout\": 3\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"bash -c 'cd \\\"${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\\\" && bash .skilled/bin/check-git-hooks.sh || { printf \\\"%s\\\\n\\\" \\\"mk-hook-drift host=codex event=SessionStart adapter=check-git-hooks.sh\\\" >&2; printf %s \\\"{\\\\\\\"hookSpecificOutput\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"hookEventName\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"SessionStart\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"additionalContext\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"mk codex hook could not resolve; build the spec-kit runtime (npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit run build) or restore the missing adapter\\\\\\\"}}\\\"; }'\",\n            \"timeout\": 3\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"bash -c 'cd \\\"${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\\\" && bash .skilled/bin/git-primary-reconcile.sh >/dev/null 2>&1 &'\",\n            \"timeout\": 3\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"bash -c 'cd \\\"${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\\\" && bash .skilled/bin/git-live-follow.sh --start || { printf \\\"%s\\\\n\\\" \\\"mk-hook-drift host=codex event=SessionStart adapter=git-live-follow.sh\\\" >&2; printf %s \\\"{\\\\\\\"hookSpecificOutput\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"hookEventName\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"SessionStart\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"additionalContext\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"mk codex hook could not resolve; build the spec-kit runtime (npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit run build) or restore the missing adapter\\\\\\\"}}\\\"; }'\",\n            \"timeout\": 3\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"bash -c 'cd \\\"${CODEX_PROJECT_DIR:-$PWD}\\\" && python3 .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/scripts/check-dist-staleness.sh --all || { printf \\\"%s\\\\n\\\" \\\"mk-hook-drift host=codex event=SessionStart adapter=check-dist-staleness.sh\\\" >&2; printf %s \\\"{\\\\\\\"hookSpecificOutput\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"hookEventName\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"SessionStart\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"additionalContext\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"mk codex hook could not resolve; build the spec-kit runtime (npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit run build) or restore the missing adapter\\\\\\\"}}\\\"; }'\",\n            \"timeout\": 5\n          }\n        ]\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"\nEach generator deletes any output it no longer expects, so a removed command or agent leaves no stale copy behind. The `config.toml` file is the one file here that no generator writes. It turns hooks on and sets up the Code Mode server.\n\n---\n\n## 2. HOW IT CONNECTS TO SKILLED\n\n| Piece | How Codex gets it |\n|---|---|\n| Instructions | The root [`AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md), the shared instruction file for every runtime |\n| Skills | No skills folder here. The advisor brief on each prompt names the skill to load, and the skill files load from `.skilled/skills/` |\n| Agents | Each shared agent as a TOML file in `agents/`, written by `sync-agents.cjs`. Each file carries the full agent text |\n| Commands | One prompt stub per command in `prompts/`, written by `sync-prompts.cjs`. A command such as `create/agent` becomes `create-agent`, and the stub tells Codex to read the canonical file in full |\n| Hooks and guards | `hooks.json`, rendered from the shared hook registry. The hooks cover the advisor, the spec-folder gate, the dispatch and MCP route guards, the post-edit checks and the session context. Each command falls back to a message when its adapter is missing |\n| Advisor | The advisor runs on the prompt hook and names the skill for each request |\n| MCP | The Code Mode server is written inline in `config.toml` |\n| Goals | No goal hook in the registry. The `create-goal` prompt authors a packet's `goal.md`, but Codex gets no session goal command here |\n| Dispatch | [`cli-codex`](../.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/README.md) hands work to Codex from another runtime. Its [hook contract](../.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/references/hook-contract.md) lists every hook a dispatched session runs |\n\n---\n\n## 3. GETTING STARTED\n\n1. Open the repository in Codex from its root. Codex reads `hooks.json` from this checkout once the checkout is trusted.\n2. Approve the hooks. Codex runs a project hook only after you approve that exact entry. Open `/hooks` in an interactive session and approve each entry it lists for review. The approval is stored as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again.\n3. Check the global file. `~/.codex/hooks.json` must hold no copy of these entries, or each hook runs twice. Run `install-codex-hooks.mjs --check` to confirm that it holds no stale copy.\n\n---\n\n## 4. WHAT IS GENERATED AND WHAT IS AUTHORED\n\n| Path | Kind | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `agents/*.toml` | Generated | Written by `sync-agents.cjs`. The sandbox mode and model settings are set here and cannot be read back into `.skilled/` |\n| `prompts/*.md` | Generated | Written by `sync-prompts.cjs`. Each stub points at its canonical command file |\n| `hooks.json` | Generated | Rendered from `hook-registry.json` by `sync-hook-registrations.cjs` |\n| `hooks/` | Links | A discovery mirror of the scripts that `hooks.json` runs |\n| `config.toml` | Authored | Turns hooks on and writes the Code Mode server inline. No generator writes it |\n| `repo-rules`, `manual-testing-playbook` | Links | The rule files and the `cli-codex` playbook |\n| `README.md`, `SYNC.md` | Authored | The documentation |\n\n**The one rule:** never edit a generated file here. Change the source in `.skilled/`, or change `hook-registry.json` for hooks, then rerun the matching generator. A hand edit to `hooks.json` is overwritten by the next sync.\n\n---\n\n## 5. CHECKING IT IS HEALTHY\n\n```bash\nnode .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-agents.cjs --check\nnode .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-prompts.cjs --check\nnode .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-hook-registrations.cjs --check\n=== hooks.json ===\n{\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"SessionStart\": [\n      {\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"comm