{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794539783908,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc256ffeoTwd6NrNr3Yljs","part":{"id":"prt_1d2e806e40014ASLwRg0ZVNnr7","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc256ffeoTwd6NrNr3Yljs","messageID":"msg_1d2e800f8001CgsZPIICmznMDi","type":"step-start","snapshot":"d0ade7cc6791d6c712e437a1c28f6effddc3edce"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794539786020,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc256ffeoTwd6NrNr3Yljs","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2e80e28001DnImE3h50Lci2m","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc256ffeoTwd6NrNr3Yljs","messageID":"msg_1d2e800f8001CgsZPIICmznMDi","type":"tool","id":"call_01_iyWtswbC6fyYPgBjby859413","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '120,150p' INSTALL-SKILLED.md; echo \"=== recommended mode ===\"; rg -n \"doctor:agents-md|embed|link\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md | head -20"},"output":"### Step 1: Run the Install Guide\n\nOpen your Skilled checkout in your runtime and run:\n\n```\n/doctor:install\n```\n\nIt asks four questions in one prompt:\n\n1. **Target repo:** the absolute path of your project.\n2. **Runtimes:** the AI coding tools you use. Pick any of `claude`, `opencode`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin` and `pi`.\n3. **Link shape:** choose `auto`. [What Gets Linked](#what-gets-linked) explains the shapes.\n4. **Instruction file:** `embed` adds the shipped sections to your project's own `AGENTS.md`. `link` points `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` at the checkout's copies.\n\n<!-- readme-check\nallow-ref CLAUDE.md | the instruction file in the operator's target repo, which this checkout does not ship\n-->\n\nThe guide writes nothing. It prints the steps below with your paths filled in.\n\n### Step 2: Run the Printed Steps\n\n| Step | Command | Run it from | What it does |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | `/doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode auto` | the checkout | Links `.skilled` and your runtime folders into the project |\n| 2 | `/doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>` | the checkout | Adds the shipped sections to your `AGENTS.md`. Skip it if you chose `link` |\n| 3 | `/doctor:mcp install` | the checkout | Builds and registers Code Mode, the bridge your runtime uses to call MCP tools |\n| 4 | `/doctor:git setup` | your project | Checks the git hooks and sk-git settings. Run `/doctor:git standards` afterwards to write repo-owned commit, PR and branch rules; until then the shipped defaults apply |\n| 5 | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` | your project | Sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server |\n| 6 | `/doctor:setup` | your project | Confirms the whole setup works |\n=== recommended mode ===\n5:This guide installs Skilled and then sets it up in your own project repositories. Section 2 installs and checks a Skilled checkout. Sections 3 and 4 bring that checkout into a project, by linking it or by copying it in.\n15:| **How it works** | Your project links to your Skilled checkout | Your project commits its own copy of Skilled |\n16:| **Updates** | One `git pull` in the checkout updates every linked project | You re-pin the copy: move it from the commit it came from to a newer one |\n17:| **Your changes** | Live in your project's own files, next to the links | Live in an overlay folder that goes back on the copy after each update |\n75:Until a local embedder model runs, the advisor matches a typed request to a command by phrase alone. With the model loaded, a command can also match by meaning, even when your request uses none of its words. The model is `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, served by Ollama on your machine, and the advisor calls it once per recommendation.\n80:/doctor:skill-advisor embedder\n89:| Disk for `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` | 274302450 bytes, about 262 MB |\n93:| Warm embedding latency | 4.8 ms median and 8.9 ms p95 over 30 calls |\n94:| Cold embedding latency | 538.53 ms for the first call |\n132:3. **Link shape:** choose `auto`. [What Gets Linked](#what-gets-linked) explains the shapes.\n133:4. **Instruction file:** `embed` adds the shipped sections to your project's own `AGENTS.md`. `link` points `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` at the checkout's copies.\n145:| 1 | `/doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode auto` | the checkout | Links `.skilled` and your runtime folders into the project |\n146:| 2 | `/doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>` | the checkout | Adds the shipped sections to your `AGENTS.md`. Skip it if you chose `link` |\n149:| 5 | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` | your project | Sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server |\n152:If you chose `link` for the instruction file, step 1 also carries `--link-instructions` and step 2 drops out.\n157:/doctor:symlink check --root <dir>\n160:Each folder should read `linked-whole` or `linked-merge`. A folder that reads `partial-merge` lacks entries the checkout gained since your last `link`. Run `link` again to add them.\n167:- **Secrets:** linking `.env` shares the checkout's secrets with every tool in the project. The plan warns you before you approve it.\n169:The link shape decides how each folder is linked:\n171:- **`whole`:** each folder becomes one link to the checkout where it can.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Step 1: Run the Install Guide\n\nOpen your Skilled checkout in your runtime and run:\n\n```\n/doctor:install\n```\n\nIt asks four questions in one prompt:\n\n1. **Target repo:** the absolute path of your project.\n2. **Runtimes:** the AI coding tools you use. Pick any of `claude`, `opencode`, `codex`, `cursor`, `devin` and `pi`.\n3. **Link shape:** choose `auto`. [What Gets Linked](#what-gets-linked) explains the shapes.\n4. **Instruction file:** `embed` adds the shipped sections to your project's own `AGENTS.md`. `link` points `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` at the checkout's copies.\n\n<!-- readme-check\nallow-ref CLAUDE.md | the instruction file in the operator's target repo, which this checkout does not ship\n-->\n\nThe guide writes nothing. It prints the steps below with your paths filled in.\n\n### Step 2: Run the Printed Steps\n\n| Step | Command | Run it from | What it does |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | `/doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode auto` | the checkout | Links `.skilled` and your runtime folders into the project |\n| 2 | `/doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>` | the checkout | Adds the shipped sections to your `AGENTS.md`. Skip it if you chose `link` |\n| 3 | `/doctor:mcp install` | the checkout | Builds and registers Code Mode, the bridge your runtime uses to call MCP tools |\n| 4 | `/doctor:git setup` | your project | Checks the git hooks and sk-git settings. Run `/doctor:git standards` afterwards to write repo-owned commit, PR and branch rules; until then the shipped defaults apply |\n| 5 | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` | your project | Sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server |\n| 6 | `/doctor:setup` | your project | Confirms the whole setup works |\n=== recommended mode ===\n5:This guide installs Skilled and then sets it up in your own project repositories. Section 2 installs and checks a Skilled checkout. Sections 3 and 4 bring that checkout into a project, by linking it or by copying it in.\n15:| **How it works** | Your project links to your Skilled checkout | Your project commits its own copy of Skilled |\n16:| **Updates** | One `git pull` in the checkout updates every linked project | You re-pin the copy: move it from the commit it came from to a newer one |\n17:| **Your changes** | Live in your project's own files, next to the links | Live in an overlay folder that goes back on the copy after each update |\n75:Until a local embedder model runs, the advisor matches a typed request to a command by phrase alone. With the model loaded, a command can also match by meaning, even when your request uses none of its words. The model is `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, served by Ollama on your machine, and the advisor calls it once per recommendation.\n80:/doctor:skill-advisor embedder\n89:| Disk for `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` | 274302450 bytes, about 262 MB |\n93:| Warm embedding latency | 4.8 ms median and 8.9 ms p95 over 30 calls |\n94:| Cold embedding latency | 538.53 ms for the first call |\n132:3. **Link shape:** choose `auto`. [What Gets Linked](#what-gets-linked) explains the shapes.\n133:4. **Instruction file:** `embed` adds the shipped sections to your project's own `AGENTS.md`. `link` points `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` at the checkout's copies.\n145:| 1 | `/doctor:symlink link --root <dir> --runtimes <list> --mode auto` | the checkout | Links `.skilled` and your runtime folders into the project |\n146:| 2 | `/doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>` | the checkout | Adds the shipped sections to your `AGENTS.md`. Skip it if you chose `link` |\n149:| 5 | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` | your project | Sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server |\n152:If you chose `link` for the instruction file, step 1 also carries `--link-instructions` and step 2 drops out.\n157:/doctor:symlink check --root <dir>\n160:Each folder should read `linked-whole` or `linked-merge`. A folder that reads `partial-merge` lacks entries the checkout gained since your last `link`. Run `link` again to add them.\n167:- **Secrets:** linking `.env` shares the checkout's secrets with every tool in the project. The plan warns you before you approve it.\n169:The link shape decides how each folder is linked:\n171:- **`whole`:** each folder becomes one link to the checkout where it can.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '120,150p' INSTALL-SKILLED.md; echo \\\"=== recommended mode ===\\\"; rg -n \\\"doctor:agents-md|embed|link\\\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794539785768,"end":1794539786020}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794539786047,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc256ffeoTwd6NrNr3Yljs","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2e80c4f00248Et5pqvzydBim","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc256ffeoTwd6NrNr3Yljs","messageID":"msg_1d2e800f8001CgsZPIICmznMDi","type":"tool","id":"call_00_NeemrqkPTFAt54CWGELl7843","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '90,115p' .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs; echo \"=== fold ===\"; sed -n '735,770p' .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs; echo \"=== check ===\"; sed -n '205,232p' .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs"},"output":"const ALLOWLIST = [\n  'AGENTS.md',\n  'CLAUDE.md',\n  '.codex/AGENTS.md',\n  '.cursor/rules/repo-local.md',\n  '.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md',\n  'REPO RULES.md',\n];\n\n// A copy at one of these paths is read for its unique lines and then removed. Every other\n// runtime-copy row is reported by the check engine and left alone here.\nconst FOLDED_COPIES = ['CLAUDE.md', '.codex/AGENTS.md'];\n\nconst USAGE = [\n  'Usage: node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs <plan|apply|restore> [options]',\n  '  plan                       compose in memory, print the targets, the diff, the new block, the',\n  '                             budget, the survival ledger and the plan digest; write nothing',\n  '  apply --plan-digest <d>    recompose, refuse a different digest, back up, then write',\n  '  restore --run=<dir>        put back exactly the files one apply recorded',\n  'Options:',\n  '  --root <dir>               compose for this repository instead of the one this script ships in',\n  '  --keep-claude-md           fold a divergent CLAUDE.md into the block but keep the file',\n  '  --remove-claude-md         fold it and remove it (the default)',\n  '  --create-router            create REPO RULES.md from the shipped rows when it is missing',\n  '  --dry-run                  print the plan and write nothing',\n  '  --yes                      take the restore confirmation as given',\n=== fold ===\n    // the proof compares occurrences, not membership, so a repeated line stays repeated.\n    const lines = localLinesOf(content, oldText === null ? '' : oldText);\n    if (lines.length > 0) {\n      chunks.push({\n        kind: 'copy',\n        path: copy.path,\n        lines: lines.length,\n        text: [`### Carried from ${copy.path}`, ...lines].join('\\n'),\n      });\n    }\n    removedCopies.push({ path: copy.path, content });\n    if (copy.path === 'CLAUDE.md' && keepClaudeMd) {\n      removedCopies.pop();\n      if (lines.length > 0) {\n        notes.push(`claude: ${copy.path} carries lines no other file has; they moved into the block and the file stays because --keep-claude-md was given`);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  const blockText = chunks.map((chunk) => chunkText(chunk.text)).filter((text) => text !== '').join('\\n\\n');\n  const composed = `${shipped}${renderBlock(markers, blockText)}`;\n\n  // The template with nothing of the repository's own in it gains nothing from the two\n  // marker lines, so that difference alone is not a reason to write: the markers appear\n  // with the first line worth keeping.\n  const templateOnly = oldText !== null && block === null && blockText === '' && oldText === shipped;\n  if (templateOnly) {\n    notes.push(`block: the template is already current and this repository carries nothing of its own, so no empty block is written`);\n  }\n\n  const files = [];\n  if (templateOnly || oldText === composed) {\n    files.push({ path: rootFile, action: 'unchanged', content: null, before: oldText });\n  } else {\n    files.push({\n      path: rootFile,\n=== check ===\n}\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 5. THE TWELVE ROWS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nfunction row(id, name, state, detail, extra = {}) {\n  return { id, name, state, detail, lines: extra.lines || [], entries: extra.entries || [] };\n}\n\n// A1. The one row an operator reads first: which of the seven shapes this repository is.\nfunction rowInstallState(context, manifest) {\n  const claudePath = path.join(context.root, 'CLAUDE.md');\n  if (!context.exists) {\n    if (fs.existsSync(claudePath)) {\n      return row('A1', 'install state', FINDING, 'claude-only',\n        { lines: [`no ${manifest.root_file}; CLAUDE.md is the only instruction file`] });\n    }\n    return row('A1', 'install state', FINDING, 'absent',\n      { lines: [`no ${manifest.root_file} and no CLAUDE.md`] });\n  }\n\n  const share = manifest.sections.length === 0 ? 0 : context.matched.length / manifest.sections.length;\n  if (share < FOREIGN_SHARE) {\n    return row('A1', 'install state', FINDING, 'foreign', {\n      lines: [\n        `${context.matched.length} of ${manifest.sections.length} shipped sections match, under the ${Math.round(FOREIGN_SHARE * 100)}% floor`,\n        'the root document is the repository\\'s own file',\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"const ALLOWLIST = [\n  'AGENTS.md',\n  'CLAUDE.md',\n  '.codex/AGENTS.md',\n  '.cursor/rules/repo-local.md',\n  '.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md',\n  'REPO RULES.md',\n];\n\n// A copy at one of these paths is read for its unique lines and then removed. Every other\n// runtime-copy row is reported by the check engine and left alone here.\nconst FOLDED_COPIES = ['CLAUDE.md', '.codex/AGENTS.md'];\n\nconst USAGE = [\n  'Usage: node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs <plan|apply|restore> [options]',\n  '  plan                       compose in memory, print the targets, the diff, the new block, the',\n  '                             budget, the survival ledger and the plan digest; write nothing',\n  '  apply --plan-digest <d>    recompose, refuse a different digest, back up, then write',\n  '  restore --run=<dir>        put back exactly the files one apply recorded',\n  'Options:',\n  '  --root <dir>               compose for this repository instead of the one this script ships in',\n  '  --keep-claude-md           fold a divergent CLAUDE.md into the block but keep the file',\n  '  --remove-claude-md         fold it and remove it (the default)',\n  '  --create-router            create REPO RULES.md from the shipped rows when it is missing',\n  '  --dry-run                  print the plan and write nothing',\n  '  --yes                      take the restore confirmation as given',\n=== fold ===\n    // the proof compares occurrences, not membership, so a repeated line stays repeated.\n    const lines = localLinesOf(content, oldText === null ? '' : oldText);\n    if (lines.length > 0) {\n      chunks.push({\n        kind: 'copy',\n        path: copy.path,\n        lines: lines.length,\n        text: [`### Carried from ${copy.path}`, ...lines].join('\\n'),\n      });\n    }\n    removedCopies.push({ path: copy.path, content });\n    if (copy.path === 'CLAUDE.md' && keepClaudeMd) {\n      removedCopies.pop();\n      if (lines.length > 0) {\n        notes.push(`claude: ${copy.path} carries lines no other file has; they moved into the block and the file stays because --keep-claude-md was given`);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  const blockText = chunks.map((chunk) => chunkText(chunk.text)).filter((text) => text !== '').join('\\n\\n');\n  const composed = `${shipped}${renderBlock(markers, blockText)}`;\n\n  // The template with nothing of the repository's own in it gains nothing from the two\n  // marker lines, so that difference alone is not a reason to write: the markers appear\n  // with the first line worth keeping.\n  const templateOnly = oldText !== null && block === null && blockText === '' && oldText === shipped;\n  if (templateOnly) {\n    notes.push(`block: the template is already current and this repository carries nothing of its own, so no empty block is written`);\n  }\n\n  const files = [];\n  if (templateOnly || oldText === composed) {\n    files.push({ path: rootFile, action: 'unchanged', content: null, before: oldText });\n  } else {\n    files.push({\n      path: rootFile,\n=== check ===\n}\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 5. THE TWELVE ROWS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nfunction row(id, name, state, detail, extra = {}) {\n  return { id, name, state, detail, lines: extra.lines || [], entries: extra.entries || [] };\n}\n\n// A1. The one row an operator reads first: which of the seven shapes this repository is.\nfunction rowInstallState(context, manifest) {\n  const claudePath = path.join(context.root, 'CLAUDE.md');\n  if (!context.exists) {\n    if (fs.existsSync(claudePath)) {\n      return row('A1', 'install state', FINDING, 'claude-only',\n        { lines: [`no ${manifest.root_file}; CLAUDE.md is the only instruction file`] });\n    }\n    return row('A1', 'install state', FINDING, 'absent',\n      { lines: [`no ${manifest.root_file} and no CLAUDE.md`] });\n  }\n\n  const share = manifest.sections.length === 0 ? 0 : context.matched.length / manifest.sections.length;\n  if (share < FOREIGN_SHARE) {\n    return row('A1', 'install state', FINDING, 'foreign', {\n      lines: [\n        `${context.matched.length} of ${manifest.sections.length} shipped sections match, under the ${Math.round(FOREIGN_SHARE * 100)}% floor`,\n        'the root document is the repository\\'s own file',\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '90,115p' .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs; echo \\\"=== fold ===\\\"; sed -n '735,770p' .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs; echo \\\"=== check ===\\\"; sed -n '205,232p' .skilled/co