{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794539836074,"sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc256ffeoTwd6NrNr3Yljs","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2e8ba11001oeFsF86q1bSCZa","sessionID":"ses_e2d1cc256ffeoTwd6NrNr3Yljs","messageID":"msg_1d2e89b47001qLwa8rmIX1AZ1k","type":"tool","id":"call_01_c11VJUODKCR2MS0ELZca8056","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-2/deep-research-strategy.md","content":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - cross-cli-2 delivery and obedience\ndescription: Segment-two cross-CLI lane for command surfacing after phases 005, 006, 008 and 010.\n---\n\n# Deep Research Strategy - cross-cli-2\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nEstablish, per runtime, whether an offered advisor command reaches the model, whether delivery is provable from a record the runtime writes, and what makes the model start the offer without an unsafe write.\n\n### Usage\n\n- Reads evidence from the parent packet (`008-command-surfacing-build`), phases 005, 006, 008, 010 and 011, and the phase 007 after arm.\n- Writes only inside this lineage directory.\n- Reducer owns Sections 3, 6, 7-11A.\n\n### Question Injection Surface\n\n`inbox.jsonl` in this lineage directory if an external question appears.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\nCross-CLI delivery, proof of delivery and obedience after phases 005, 006, 008 and 010: per-runtime evidence that an offered command reaches the model, that delivery is provable from a committed record, and that the model takes the offer without an unsafe write.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] Which runtime loses the Gate 2 policy before the model sees it, and which single file per runtime decides that: Codex's hook approval key, Claude's instruction file, or the shared session readers?\n- [ ] Can brief delivery be proven for every runtime from a record the runtime itself writes, and what exactly must be recorded at hook time?\n- [ ] Why do 4 unsafe runs remain, and are they delivery failures, obedience failures, or routing deferrals?\n- [ ] What makes a model emit the COMMAND: line or take an offered command, and which contract change raises obedience without raising false offers?\n- [ ] Which change per runtime raises measured starts for the least risk to the floors (typed recall 24 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, scorer [159,50,20,5])?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Re-recommending anything phases 005, 006, 008, 010 or 011 built or plans.\n- Implementing any fix (research only).\n- The offer-rate and semantic-lane angle owned by the offer-reach lineage.\n- Brief wording, byte cost and install UX owned by the ux-cost-2 lineage, except where they change delivery or obedience.\n- Starting CLI, arena or daemon sessions; running ollama; editing anything outside this lineage.\n- Reading or printing holdout prompt text from `command-prompts.jsonl`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Max 4 iterations, convergence threshold 0.05 after the 3-iteration floor.\n- Stop early only at legal convergence; record the reason in research.md.\n- No writes outside this lineage directory; spec.md writeback and continuity save are deferred and recorded as scope decisions.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n[None yet]\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nQ1: Which runtime loses the Gate 2 policy before the model sees it, and which single file per runtime decides that: Codex's hook approval key, Claude's instruction file, or the shared session readers?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\nEvidence pointers (read-only):\n\n- Parent packet `008-command-surfacing-build`: `goal.md` log (after-arm numbers, unsafe-row reasons), `spec.md`, `decision-record.md`.\n- Phase `009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md` (segment one, 14 ranked recommendations) and `spec.md` dispositions.\n- Phase implementations: `005-recommendation-contract-and-brief`, `006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers`, `008-embedder-setup-and-cost`, `010-reachability-and-attribution` implementation summaries.\n- Phase `011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/spec.md` and `tasks.md` (in build; do not re-recommend).\n- After arm: `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre-final.jsonl`, `runs-post-final.jsonl`, `runs-g2.jsonl`, `runs-post-claude-bullet.jsonl`, scored with `score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary`.\n- Delivery code: `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs`, `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/`, `command-prompts.jsonl` (tune and none rows only).\n- Runtime surfaces: `.codex/README.md`, `.codex/hooks.json`, `.claude/settings.json`, `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/`, `.pi/extensions/prompt-advisor.ts`.\n- Install path: `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs`.\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Source pointers: hook brief renderer, per-runtime hooks and plugins, shared session readers, offer replay and backfill, behaviour runner.\n- Reuse candidates: `command-offer.mjs` replay and `briefDelivered`, the committed scorer, `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs`.\n- Integration points: hook registration per runtime, session stores, run-log fields, scorer attribution.\n- Constraints: read-only git, no CLI sessions, no ollama, no writes outside the lineage.\n\n---\n\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n- Max iterations: 4\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: true\n- research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred)\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `.deep-research-pause`\n- Current generation: 1\n- Started: 2026-11-13T04:20:00.000Z\n"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-2/deep-research-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-2/deep-research-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-2/deep-research-strategy.md\", \"content\": \"---\\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - cross-cli-2 delivery and obedience\\ndescription: Segment-two cross-CLI lane for command surfacing after phases 005, 006, 008 and 010.\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Research Strategy - cross-cli-2\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nEstablish, per runtime, whether an offered advisor command reaches the model, whether delivery is provable from a record the runtime writes, and what makes the model start the offer without an unsafe write.\\n\\n### Usage\\n\\n- Reads evidence from the parent packet (`008-command-surfacing-build`), phases 005, 006, 008, 010 and 011, and the phase 007 after arm.\\n- Writes only inside this lineage directory.\\n- Reducer owns Sections 3, 6, 7-11A.\\n\\n### Question Injection Surface\\n\\n`inbox.jsonl` in this lineage directory if an external question appears.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\nCross-CLI delivery, proof of delivery and obedience after phases 005, 006, 008 and 010: per-runtime evidence that an offered command reaches the model, that delivery is provable from a committed record, and that the model takes the offer without an unsafe write.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\\n- [ ] Which runtime loses the Gate 2 policy before the model sees it, and which single file per runtime decides that: Codex's hook approval key, Claude's instruction file, or the shared session readers?\\n- [ ] Can brief delivery be proven for every runtime from a record the runtime itself writes, and what exactly must be recorded at hook time?\\n- [ ] Why do 4 unsafe runs remain, and are they delivery failures, obedience failures, or routing deferrals?\\n- [ ] What makes a model emit the COMMAND: line or take an offered command, and which contract change raises obedience without raising false offers?\\n- [ ] Which change per runtime raises measured starts for the least risk to the floors (typed recall 24 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, scorer [159,50,20,5])?\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- Re-recommending anything phases 005, 006, 008, 010 or 011 built or plans.\\n- Implementing any fix (research only).\\n- The offer-rate and semantic-lane angle owned by the offer-reach lineage.\\n- Brief wording, byte cost and install UX owned by the ux-cost-2 lineage, except where they change delivery or obedience.\\n- Starting CLI, arena or daemon sessions; running ollama; editing anything outside this lineage.\\n- Reading or printing holdout prompt text from `command-prompts.jsonl`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Max 4 iterations, convergence threshold 0.05 after the 3-iteration floor.\\n- Stop early only at legal convergence; record the reason in research.md.\\n- No writes outside this lineage directory; spec.md writeback and continuity save are deferred and recorded as scope decisions.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Saturated: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\\n[None yet]\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\\nQ1: Which runtime loses the Gate 2 policy before the model sees it, and which single file per runtime decides that: Codex's hook approval key, Claude's instruction file, or the shared session readers?\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\nEvidence pointers (read-only):\\n\\n- Parent packet `008-command-surfacing-build`: `goal.md` log (after-arm numbers, unsafe-row reasons), `spec.md`, `decision-record.md`.\\n- Phase `009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md` (segment one, 14 ranked recommendations) and `spec.md` dispositions.\\n- Phase implementations: `005-recommendation-contract-and-brief`, `006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers`, `008-embedder-setup-and-cost`, `010-reachability-and-attribution` implementation summaries.\\n- Phase `011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/spec.md` and `tasks.md` (in build; do not re-recommend).\\n- After arm: `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre-final.jsonl`, `runs-post-final.jsonl`, `runs-g2.jsonl`, `runs-post-claude-bullet.jsonl`, scored with `score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary`.\\n- Delivery code: `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs`, `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/`, `command-prompts.jsonl` (tune and none rows only).\\n- Runtime surfaces: `.codex/README.md`, `.codex/hooks.json`, `.claude/settings.json`, `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, `.dsh/plugins/repo-guards/`, `.pi/extensions/prompt-advisor.ts`.\\n- Install path: `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs`.\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- Source pointers: hook brief renderer, per-runtime hooks and plugins, shared session readers, offer replay and backfill, behaviour runner.\\n- Reuse candidates: `command-offer.mjs` replay and `briefDelivered`, the committed scorer, `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs`.\\n- Integration points: hook registration per runtime, session stores, run-log fields, scorer attribution.\\n- Constraints: read-only git, no CLI sessions, no ollama, no writes outside the lineage.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\\n- Max iterations: 4\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\\n- Progressive synthesis: true\\n- research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred)\\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `.deep-research-pause`\\n- Current generation: 1\\n- Started: 2026-11-13T04:20:00.000Z\\n\"}"},"time":{"start":1794539829777,"end":1794539836074}}}}
